  "conclusions": [
    "Exact current on_object_destroyed system name binds registration through vtable/run wrapper to native14118d7f0.",
    "Non-item destroy removes GUID from live index and queues command14094ac80. That command calls14116d5f0.",
    "At14116d5f0, presence of typed DespawnAnimAnnounced selects PendingDestroy insertion; absence selects1410d88d0 immediately. This is a presence test, not removal of the marker.",
    "1410d88d0 calls Guid registrar1404aba80 and removes that component, then initializes default fade with f32 -1 and inserts DespawnFade using registrar1404a3930.",
    "The separate current explicit GO animation handler handles0x43 custom and0x44 despawn event variants;0x44 queues DespawnAnimAnnounced(false) via callback14095ba90. The current destroy handler does not queue that callback.",
    "The current tick-filtered marker consumer1409dadb0 writes packed Some(157) atGoAnim+0x2c, the Despawn one-shot, not Open148.",
    "For fresh ordinary cache objects without a prior explicit despawn-announcement marker, the AS DestroyObject-only route initiates Guid removal/DespawnFade, with no recovered hidden lid-open or new one-shot157 request."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "The native marker branch fixture uses synthetic alive/generation metadata and intercepts PendingDestroy registration and the immediate teardown helper at their entry; it does not execute generic ECS migration/hooks.",
    "Ghidra bounded raw imports omit PE-wide callers/types and external helper bodies. Exact typed registry names/constants and direct calls are verified separately from the whole installed target.",
    "Known queued-command/component operations and direct typed paths are recovered. Generic ECS hooks, fade timing, model animation callbacks, scheduler execution and prior explicit announcement states are not certified.",
    "No Rust compilation/execution, game launch, real model/MPQ or original/rebuilt rendering comparison. No new cache source gap is demonstrated by this bounded consumer trace."
  ],
